summary:
  The settle round's flatness gate goes blind — a warming ramp becomes a
  full-size correction again.

history:
  Watched live 2026-08-10, twice in one morning: after a rebuild the
  Bluetooth offset readings RISE about ten milliseconds a minute for
  minutes on end (-36 -28 -8, then +7 +19). Adjacent readings on a ramp
  agree with each other while both are wrong together, and the +13 the
  first pair-based version produced put a room the listener had just
  called good audibly out of step. First-against-last flatness is the one
  comparison a steady ramp cannot pass — this mutant raises that gate out
  of reach, which is exactly the bug shipping a "small cleanup" to the
  threshold would reintroduce.

  Anchor rewritten 2026-08-12: the refusal branch grew a body (it now
  records the three readings and the spread, so a give-up carries its own
  evidence into the journal), and the one-line form the anchor bit on no
  longer exists. Same gate, same swap, shorter bite — the condition alone.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
              if (hi - lo > _settleFlatMs) {

replace:
              if (hi - lo > 9999999) {

expect:
  Killed by tst_syncengine.qml
  test_a_warming_ramp_cannot_become_a_correction: the ramp 7/19/31 then
  passes as flat, the median acts, the map moves off 145 and the test
  goes red. Line-neutral on purpose — SyncEngine.qml is not ratcheted,
  but a kill must come from the behavioural test, not a size lock.
